  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contracting in North Dakota remains concentrated. Total obligations reached $754M in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell down 8.2% year over year. Award volume totaled 2,350 awards, with an average award size of $321K. Obligations by fiscal year show variability, including $780M in FY21, $973M in FY22, $803M in FY23, $980M in FY24, and $821M in FY25. The Department of Health and Human Services led buyers with $351M, followed by the Department of Defense with $187M and the Department of Transportation with $88.1M. NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC was the largest vendor with $329M in obligations, followed by WALSH FEDERAL LLC with $74.4M and PACKET DIGITAL LLC with $36.8M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers dominated industries at $292M, while Commercial and Institutional Building Construction totaled $127M. The data cover contract obligations and reflect partial totals for the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies drove most federal obligations in North Dakota?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $351M, making it the largest buyer. The Department of Defense obligated $187M and the Department of Transportation obligated $88.1M. Several civilian agencies and small-dollar buyers also appear, including the Department of Veterans Affairs with $40.2M and the Department of Agriculture with $31.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who captured the largest federal awards in North Dakota and which industries dominate?",
        "body": "NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC received $329M in obligations, the largest vendor total. WALSH FEDERAL LLC received $74.4M and PACKET DIGITAL LLC received $36.8M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers accounted for $292M by industry, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounted for $127M."
      }
    ]
  },
